{"packet_id":"D052-01","doc_id":"D052","jurisdiction":"MA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Massachusetts security deposit cap","requirement":"A lessor may not require a tenant or prospective tenant to pay a security deposit larger than the first month's rent, and may not at any time after the tenancy begins demand advance rent above the current month's rent.","key_value":"1 month's rent","coverage_conditions":"Leases and tenancies of residential real property in Massachusetts, including demands made by the lessor's agent.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":"2025-08-01","citation":"G.L. c. 186, § 15B","quoted_span":"(iii) a security deposit equal to the first month's rent provided that such security deposit is deposited as required by subsection (3) and that the tenant is given the statement of condition as required by subsection (2)","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D052-01","doc_id":"D052","jurisdiction":"MA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Security deposit interest and separate account","requirement":"A lessor holding a security deposit for a year or longer must pay interest at 5% per year, or the lesser bank rate, from the first day of tenancy, and must keep the deposit in a separate interest-bearing account.","key_value":"5% per year","coverage_conditions":"Security deposits for residential tenancies in Massachusetts held one year or longer from the start of the term.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":"Failure to place the deposit in a separate account entitles the tenant to immediate return of the deposit.","effective_date":null,"citation":"G.L. c. 186, § 15B","quoted_span":"A lessor of residential real property who holds a security deposit pursuant to this section for a period of one year or longer from the commencement of the term of the tenancy shall, beginning with the first day of the tenancy, pay interest at the rate of five per cent per year","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D052-01","doc_id":"D052","jurisdiction":"MA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Security deposit return deadline and damages","requirement":"A lessor must return the security deposit or its balance within 30 days after the tenancy ends, with an itemized, sworn list of any deductions; violations can bring triple damages plus costs and attorney's fees.","key_value":"30 days","coverage_conditions":"All residential tenancies in Massachusetts, including tenancies at will and written leases.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":"Three times the security deposit or balance to which the tenant is entitled, plus 5% interest, court costs and reasonable attorney's fees.","effective_date":null,"citation":"G.L. c. 186, § 15B","quoted_span":"The lessor shall, within thirty days after the termination of occupancy under a tenancy-at-will or the end of the tenancy as specified in a valid written lease agreement, return to the tenant the security deposit or any balance thereof","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D052-01","doc_id":"D052","jurisdiction":"MA","category":"application_screening_fees","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Massachusetts cap on upfront tenant payments","requirement":"At or before the tenancy starts, a lessor or the lessor's agent may not require payment beyond first month's rent, last month's rent at the same rate, a one-month security deposit, and the cost of a key and lock.","key_value":"first + last month's rent + 1 month deposit + key/lock cost","coverage_conditions":"All residential tenancies in Massachusetts; applies to the lessor and to any agent of the lessor.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":"2025-08-01","citation":"G.L. c. 186, § 15B","quoted_span":"(i) rent for the first full month of occupancy;  and, (ii) rent for the last full month of occupancy calculated at the same rate as the first month;  and, (iii) a security deposit equal to the first month's rent","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D052-01","doc_id":"D052","jurisdiction":"MA","category":"application_screening_fees","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Fee-in-lieu-of-deposit cap","requirement":"Where regulations authorize a fee instead of a security deposit, the total fees may not exceed 1 month's rent, and the tenant must be allowed to choose a full security deposit instead of the fee.","key_value":"1 month's rent","coverage_conditions":"Residential tenancies in Massachusetts where the executive office of housing and livable communities authorizes a fee in lieu of a security deposit.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":"The fee must be optional for both tenant and lessor; the tenant may opt out by paying the full deposit.","penalty":null,"effective_date":"2025-08-01","citation":"G.L. c. 186, § 15B","quoted_span":"(C) limit the total sum of the fee or recurring payments, regardless of the duration of the lease and any extensions thereto, to an amount not to exceed 1 month's rent","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D052-01","doc_id":"D052","jurisdiction":"MA","category":"screening_restrictions","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Fee-in-lieu option must be offered regardless of income or credit score","requirement":"A lessor offering a fee in lieu of a security deposit must offer it to every approved prospective tenant regardless of income, race, gender, gender identity, disability, sexual orientation, immigration status, household size or credit score, and may not set the fee using those factors.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Lessors who offer a fee in lieu of a security deposit to prospective tenants whose applications for occupancy have been approved.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":"2025-08-01","citation":"G.L. c. 186, § 15B","quoted_span":"(I) to offer the option of a fee in lieu of a security deposit to every prospective tenant whose application for occupancy has been approved, regardless of income, race, gender, gender identity, disability, sexual orientation, immigration status, size of household or credit score;  and (II) not to consider such factors and categories when setting the amount of the fee","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
